# boundary_worker (Resource)

{{ .Description | trimspace }}

## Example Usage

### Controller-led worker

{{tffile "examples/resources/boundary_worker/controller_led.tf"}}

Use controller-led registration when Terraform can deliver a generated activation
token to the worker. Omit `worker_generated_auth_token`.

### Worker-led worker

{{tffile "examples/resources/boundary_worker/worker_led.tf"}}

Use worker-led registration when the worker generates the authorization request.
Set `worker_generated_auth_token` to the generated token.

### No managed worker resource

Without a `boundary_worker` resource, Terraform does not manage a worker.

### Both registration methods

Configure separate `boundary_worker` resources when your deployment requires
both registration methods.

{{tffile "examples/resources/boundary_worker/both.tf"}}

Refer to the [register workers](https://developer.hashicorp.com/boundary/docs/workers/registration)
documentation to learn about worker registration.

